      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1898 extension of the railroad from Aberdeen to Hoquiam boosted logging and lumber, cementing the town’s economic foundation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hoquiam%2C_Washington",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hoquiam once hosted Minor League teams like the Loggers and the Grays Harbor Ports, keeping baseball alive in the Pacific Northwest.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
